Measurement of inclusive forward \(\pi^{0}\) production in the first polarized p-p collision at \(\sqrt{s}=200\) GeV was achieved using a prototype Forward (neutral) Pion Detector. The invariant differential cross section was consistent with next-to-leading order perturbative QCD calculation. Large positive analyzing power was found for large Feynman-x (\(x_{F}>0.3\)). In addition, a new analysis program was developed for the upgraded Forward Pion Detector (FPD).

