## Appendix A Shower-shape Pb-glass Response Simulation

Steve Heppelmann of Penn. State University provided a simple FPD Pb-glass tower responses simulation based on Pb-glass shower-shape functions [36]. The functions are Equations 3.5 and 3.6. For simplicity, only pure \(\pi^{0}\rightarrow\gamma\gamma\) decay events were generated. This was not full simulation by all means, but the event characteristics was not unlike the real data (when we selected events that were most likely \(\pi^{0}\)), and it was simple and provided us with a way to inter-compare our event reconstruction algorithm with simulation input.

Generated \(pi^{0}\) has a \(\theta\) distribution that is 15% of Gaussian around \(\theta_{0}\) with \(\sigma=0.00236\) radian and 85% of exponential \(\exp^{-(\theta-\theta_{0})/\lambda}\) with \(\lambda=0.02\). The angle \(\theta_{0}\) is the \(\theta\) angle from the center of West-South FPD module to STAR IP. The \(\phi\) distribution is flat. The energy distribution of \(\pi^{0}\) is exponential. Then we require that both photons from the decay are contained within a certain fiducial volume at FPD West-South location. Responses from each individual tower are calculated using the default shower-shape. The ADC counts are randomized using a Gaussian distribution around the calculated value, with \(\sigma=15\%\times\sqrt{E}\), where \(E\) is the calculated energy deposit in the tower in GeV. An ADC roundoff is applied to get the final simulated ADCcounts.

We used the same default shower shape function for the analysis of this simulation data. Since in this case we know we have used the "correct" shower shape, let's see what the position reconstruction looks like (Figure A.1).

We can see that if we only look at data within a slightly tighter fiducial volume than the FPD module itself, the difference is not big (again, we should also ignore those spikes that are located exactly at the center of towers, as ex

Figure A.1: Comparison of reconstructed and simulated \(y_{\gamma}\) distribution using default shower shape.

plained in the shower shape discussion in Chapter 2). The morale is, if we find a good shower shape, we should expect a reasonable position reconstruction.

