**Vita**

Yiqun Wang was born in Guiyang, Guizhou Province, China on January 14, 1971, the son of Xiang-hong Wang and Su-zen Yuan. He received the Bachelor of Science degree in Physics from Peking University, Beijing, China in July 1991. He went back to his hometown, and worked in Guizhou Institue of Transportation for the next several years. In the meaning, he brushed up his English skills and took the TOEFL and GRE tests. Then he applied to the University of Texas at Austin for enrollment in their physics program. He was accepted and started graduate studies in August, 1994. At first, he majored in theoretical physics, string theory in particular. In 2000, he transferred to high energy nuclear physics, and participated in BNL's RHIC run FY02 and FY03 as a member of the STAR collaboration.

